rful charisma while writers  and directors made sure to stay true to  dr. Seuss's original version many  changes were made however these  altercations were mostly added to  elongate the movie screen time after all  dr. Seuss's book was only 69 page  long as many of you surely remember the  Grinch's heart is two sizes too small  which makes it impossible for emotions  like love and hope to settle in as a  result the Grinch becomes a hermit who  lives in a lonely cave on Mount crumpit  it is here that he looks down at  Whoville and Spears and discussed  knowing that December 25th is quickly  approaching whenever cheerful noises  start to emanate from the city center in  this book The Grinch sneaks into the  city on Christmas Eve and steals every  last present in Whoville he dresses up  as Santa Claus and forces his dog masks  to pull a sleigh filled with gifts all  the way up to his lair unfortunately max  is unable to carry up tasks  causing the Grinch to get stranded  Midway up Mount crumpit as the Sun rises  he waits for Whoville to be filled with  cries of sorrow but instead his ears  filled with Christmas carols at this  moment he realizes that the Christmas  spirit has nothing to do with presents  causing his heart to grow three times  bigger how the grinch came to be most  writers don't like to admit it but their  main characters tend to be based off of  themselves luckily dr. Seuss is not like  most writers which is why he admitted  that the Grinch was loosely based off  with himself  however this connection was only made  after the book was written and released  on the day after Christmas dr. Seuss was  brushing his teeth when he caught a  glimpse of the Grinch in the mirror it  was then that he realized that he needed  to rediscover the meaning of Christmas  once more funny enough his very own  stepdaughter confirmed this notion when  she stated that her stepfather was the  Grinch during his sour moments and the  cat from The Cat in the Hat  during his good 